<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The crisis gripping Nvidia is gathering pa=
ce, with about $430bn (=C2=A3322bn) wiped off the value of the world=E2=80=
=99s most valuable company since it was hit by a spying scandal.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Overnight, Nvidia announced it had hired a=
 former top federal prosecutor to help investigate the chief executive Jens=
en Huang=E2=80=99s relationship with a suspected Chinese spy.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The company=E2=80=99s board have retained =
Joon H Kim, the former acting US Attorney of the southern district of New Y=
ork, and his firm Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen &amp; Katz to conduct =E2=80=9Ca =
thorough and independent investigation=E2=80=9D.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Wachtell is a heavyweight corporate law fi=
rm. In 2022 it was hired by Twitter to force Elon Musk to complete his $44b=
n takeover, for example, and has a track record of advising major companies=
 on issues such as mergers and corporate governance.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">It will now look into the circumstances of=
 Huang=E2=80=99s affair =E2=80=93 thought to be with Alice Huang, who worke=
d for the Nvidia customer Megaspeed and who US officials believe is a Chine=
se spy.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Although Beijing has denied allegations th=
at it operated an espionage operation targeting Jensen Huang, Nvidia=E2=80=
=99s value has been buffeted this week.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Yesterday its shares fell by almost 5.5%, =
adding to the 4.27% drop on Monday. This has pulled the company=E2=80=99s v=
alue down to $4.07tn, from $4.50tn before the story broke last weekend.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The allegations over <a href=3D"https://ab=
link.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgs=
zcCSneHEBUsSd6DY9A_zGHjXnJyBTsjfyKRnviVI97-dF2T9L5KYTuT46tKAGkN5Q2itwOJl6p2=
AOtElZk56rOptFn1D5PBT3BhnHxz6REKrVBefsCvxFt_URyUsQCZ8ClIxW0OqN8ixaIXxT2qMJV=
2h06DJyDL6hJ5hzDUshbgdAWPGzQUntzNgmpmRCvT2x8d5pkgTY/4vn/GcCxhrkFReaoq_L8q_s=
UOQ/h30/h001.ETOM02FF9pLrguxMTMYvsL105zAQmAkElTrdaxYnXx8" style=3D"color: #=
0077B6;">Nvidia</a> are testing relations between Washington and Beijing, a=
ccording to the top US diplomat in China.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The ambassador David Perdue told Bloomberg=
 Television: =E2=80=9CThe situation with Nvidia is another reminder that we=
 have to stay diligent.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CNational security is part of this=
 economic conversation because economic security is national security. And =
so, what we=E2=80=99re doing with China is bumpy right now.=E2=80=9D</p>
